.el .ds Aq '
.TH voltkit-using 1  "Voltkit 0.9.1" "Voltkit Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
voltkit\-using \- Show which programs keep a file, folder, drive or network port busy
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvoltkit using\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITARGET\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show which programs keep a file, folder, drive or network port busy
.PP
TARGET is a path, or a port number such as 3000. Lists each program with its PID and how it uses the target. Only your own programs can be checked as a normal user; run it with sudo to include other users\*(Aq programs and system services.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fITARGET\fR>
A file, folder or mount point, or a port number
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Find what keeps a USB drive busy:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBvoltkit using /media/$USER/USB\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Find the program on port 3000:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBvoltkit using 3000\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Include system services:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBsudo voltkit using 80\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Ask a program to quit, then force it if it won\*(Aqt:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBkill PID
kill \-KILL PID\fR
.fi
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBvoltkit\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
